# CloudScope GitHub Actions Workflow

Location:

```text
.github/workflows/deploy.yml
```

## Workflow Configuration

```yaml
name: Deploy CloudScope

on:
  push:
    branches:
      - main

jobs:
  deploy:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest

    steps:
      - name: Checkout Repository
        uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Show Repository Contents
        run: |
          pwd
          ls -la

      - name: Configure SSH Key
        run: |
          mkdir -p ~/.ssh
          echo "${{ secrets.EC2_SSH_KEY }}" > ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
          chmod 600 ~/.ssh/id_ed25519

      - name: Deploy CloudScope
        run: |
          ssh -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no \
          -i ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 \
          ${{ secrets.EC2_USER }}@${{ secrets.EC2_HOST }} "
            cd ~/cloudscope &&
            git pull &&
            source venv/bin/activate &&
            pip install -r requirements.txt &&
            sudo systemctl restart cloudscope &&
            sudo systemctl status cloudscope --no-pager
          "
```

---

## Required Repository Secrets

```text
EC2_HOST
EC2_USER
EC2_SSH_KEY
```

### EC2_HOST

Public IP address of the CloudScope EC2 instance.

### EC2_USER

Linux user account used for deployment.

```text
ec2-user
```

### EC2_SSH_KEY

Private deployment key used by GitHub Actions to authenticate to the EC2 instance.

---

## Deployment Flow

```text
Developer
    ↓
git push
    ↓
GitHub Actions
    ↓
SSH Authentication
    ↓
EC2 Instance
    ↓
git pull
    ↓
Install Dependencies
    ↓
Restart CloudScope
    ↓
Verify Service Status
```